Done. Delivered:

**`ring.go`** — `NewRing(capacity)` returns `(*Ring, error)`, error on ≤0. Ring implements `slog.Handler` with concurrent-safe ring buffer. `Records()` returns deep-copied slice, oldest first, evicting oldest at capacity. `WithAttrs`/`WithGroup` return a `ringHandler` wrapper that tracks nested group/attr interleaving correctly.

**`fanout.go`** — `New(handlers ...slog.Handler) (*slog.Logger, error)` errors on empty; uses `slog.NewMultiHandler` (Go 1.26 built-in) for fan-out when >1 handler.

**`logfan_test.go`** — 16 tests covering:
- NewRing boundary errors
- Empty ring, single record, ordering, eviction, copy semantics
- `Enabled` all levels
- WithAttrs / WithGroup delegation
- Concurrent writes and concurrent read/write
- New: empty-error, single handler, fan-out to two rings, attrs preservation across fan-out

`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` all pass. No third-party deps.
